{
  "title": "Use learned ingredient names for read-time derived grams",
  "description": "RecipeResponse.derived_measurements (server/src/models.rs derived_measurements -> ramekin_core::derived_grams) resolves densities through the committed catalog only (catalog::line_grams_per_cup). \
Calorie estimates also consult learned names (catalog::line_grams_per_cup_with with ingredient_names::load_learned), so a name the LLM mapped to a catalog entry ('heaping cups of AP flour' -> 'all-purpose flour') gets calories but no gram amount.\n\
\n\
Load the learned map for a recipe's items on GET /api/recipes/{id} and POST /api/import/text, and pass it through derived_grams. \
Learned estimates (LearnedTarget::Estimate) must stay excluded, as the catalog README says. \
Watch the read path's query count (one extra indexed lookup per recipe read). \
The iOS offline cache stores no derived grams (it only feeds local search), so no cache invalidation is needed. \
No pipeline impact.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
